                "entry_id": "d7a879b0-a7e8-3844-a851-c7ec26bd7c82",
                "word": "psilocybin",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "e5cc2e55-b50c-4f25-b27b-a76cf6ec2b66",
                        "entry_id": "d7a879b0-a7e8-3844-a851-c7ec26bd7c82",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "psilocybins"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "2b558a75-bea7-3597-83bd-2d463f473352",
                        "entry_id": "d7a879b0-a7e8-3844-a851-c7ec26bd7c82",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A hallucinogenic alkaloid, C₁₂H₁₅N₂O·H₂PO₃, present in several species of Central American mushroom and producing effects similar to LSD. The prodrug of psilocin."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "157b065e-0aec-473b-b3d3-d69042b36db7",
                                "sense_id": "2b558a75-bea7-3597-83bd-2d463f473352",
                                "text": "The problem of the mushroom supply was solved straight away when Leary learned from a graduate student named George Litwin that a chemist at the Sandoz Corporation, Dr. Albert Hofmann, had recently synthesized the psychoactive molecule of the mushroom, calling it psilocybin."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7e05137a-6ad8-44f0-a85d-e036765efb15",
                                "sense_id": "2b558a75-bea7-3597-83bd-2d463f473352",
                                "text": "It’s no stretch to posit that because human neurotransmitters respond to the platform’s iconic use of a certain shade of blue, and spark with dopamine upon receiving a “like” or “tag” notification, desperate children are now living in cages and a raving madman occupies the Oval Office. Not even Orwell, after a feast of psilocybin, could have predicted this dystopia."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "e8769b37-46e8-4c45-a611-86fe97c3eb74",
                        "source_entry_id": "d7a879b0-a7e8-3844-a851-c7ec26bd7c82",
                        "source_sense_id": "2b558a75-bea7-3597-83bd-2d463f473352",
                        "source_sense_description": "hallucinogenic alkaloid",
                        "target_lang_word": "psilocybine",
                        "target_lang_code": "nl",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "psilocybine",
                                "target_lang_code": "nl",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b5cc61a2-4682-3833-a6a6-b1c6e492d868",
                                        "entry_id": "a30f69ac-40e8-3fcc-8f56-fba3a646524e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "de belangrijkste psychoactieve stof uit verschillende hallucinogene paddenstoelsoorten"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "97a89c1b-a124-4a49-ba70-89f58739edb9",
                                                "sense_id": "b5cc61a2-4682-3833-a6a6-b1c6e492d868",
                                                "text": "De stof psilocybine, aanwezig in tientallen verboden paddenstoelen met een hallucinerende werking, kan depressie mogelijk helpen behandelen"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "85874edc-28f2-4a45-b850-e21358363c42",
                        "source_entry_id": "d7a879b0-a7e8-3844-a851-c7ec26bd7c82",
                        "source_sense_id": "2b558a75-bea7-3597-83bd-2d463f473352",
                        "source_sense_description": "hallucinogenic alkaloid",
                        "target_lang_word": "psilocybine",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "psilocybine",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c7602247-24b7-3b6d-985c-e8e5472da9fa",
                                        "entry_id": "10061afc-afef-39a3-be7d-4661d94b1212",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Ester d’acide phosphorique, principe actif de certains champignons hallucinogènes."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "556fc6cb-b857-4fdd-b01c-dc8058d18365",
                                                "sense_id": "c7602247-24b7-3b6d-985c-e8e5472da9fa",
                                                "text": "Cette pratique l’a conduit à se replonger dans la littérature des années 1950 et 1960 sur les hallucinogènes classiques (mescaline, psilocybine, LSD)."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ee3bedda-6044-46ce-9d10-d4f6b38f3c53",
                                                "sense_id": "c7602247-24b7-3b6d-985c-e8e5472da9fa",
                                                "text": "La psilocybine est la principale substance psychoactive des champignons hallucinogènes. Après ingestion, elle est transformée en une forme pharmacologiquement active, la psilocine."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1c2cf289-2204-4428-a2c2-cb86053f525d",
                                                "sense_id": "c7602247-24b7-3b6d-985c-e8e5472da9fa",
                                                "text": "La thérapie assistée par psychédéliques consiste à prendre une dose de substance psychotrope — du LSD, de l’ecstasy ou de la psilocybine, le principe actif de certains champignons hallucinogènes — sous le contrôle d’au moins un soignant, à l’hôpital."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
